## Step 3a (9/14/26): baseline 0DTE quotes -- `pull_baseline_quotes.py` (Zach runs it from Git Bash)

Goal: a "normalized baseline price of OTM options" per name so each event's strangle cost can be expressed as a
multiple of the name's own normal Friday. For every event, the 5 Fridays strictly before eff_date (rolled to the
prior trading day on holidays; MRVL's Thursday eff date still maps to Fridays) get the same pull as the event day:
0DTE chain, strikes within 8% of the 15:00 spot, 15:00-16:00 at 1s -> t_opra_quotes via pull_0dte_quotes.pull_pair.
Names without weeklies only have a chain on the monthly inside the window; other Fridays log `no_chain`.
Spot snaps 15:00/15:10/.../15:40 + PX_LAST per baseline day -> `baseline_spots.csv`; checkpoints ->
`_baseline_pull_meta.csv`. 19 events x 5 = 95 pairs; ~1 min per pair with a chain.
Pull result (9/14/26): 91 of 95 pairs ok, every name had weekly 0DTE chains; 4 `no_spot` (CRH 11/28/25 and WDAY
11/29/24 are Black Friday half-days, UBER 12/1 + 12/8/23 no prints).

